3 by the ones place digit **0** of 30:  \n   \\( 63 \\times 0 = 0 \\).  \n2. Multiply 63 by the tens place digit **30** (or equivalently, \\( 63 \\times 3 \\times 10 \\)):  \n   First, calculate \\( 63 \\times 3 = 189 \\), then shift one place left (multiply by 10):  \n   \\( 189 \\times 10 = 1890 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 0 + 1890 = 1890 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **1890**.  \n\nThe initial answer of 1190 is incorrect because \\( 63 \\times 3 = 189 \\), not 119. The correct calculation follows the steps above.",
