 .\n2 + 3 = 5.  .\n3 + 6 = 9.  .\n6 + 0 (since 632 doesn't have a thousands place beyond the first digit) = 6. Wait, actually, 6320 is 6 thousands, 3 hundreds, 2 tens, 0 ones. Adding 632 which is 0 thousands, 6 hundreds, 3 tens, 2 ones. So when adding:.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 0 = 6.  .\nHundreds place: 3 + 6 = 9.  .\nTens place: 2 + 3 = 5.  .\nOnes place: 0 + 2 = 2. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
