wo results: 292 (from the ones place) and 5110 (from the tens place). Adding them together: 292 + 5110. Let's see, 292 + 5000 is 5292, then plus 110 more? Wait no, 5110 is 5000+110. Wait, 292 +5110. Let me line them up:.\n\n  292.\n+5110.\n------.\n?.\n\nStarting from the right, 2 +0=2, 9+1=10, write down 0 and carry 1. Then 2 +1 (the carried 1) is 3, plus the 1 from the 5110's hundreds place? Wait, maybe I should do it properly:.\n\nActually, 292 is 0292, so:.\n\n   0292.\n+5110.\n------.\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n2 + 0 = 2.\n9 + 1 = 10, write 0, carryover 1.\n2 + 1 (from the next digit) plus the carried 1: Wait, maybe I'm confused. Let me think again. Wait 5110 is written as 5 thousands, 1 hundred, 1 ten, 0 ones. So:.\n\nThousands place: 5.\nHundreds place:1.\nTens place:1.\nOnes place:0.\n\nAdding to 292 (which is 0 thousands, 2 hundreds, 9 tens, 2 ones):.\n\nAdding:.\n\nOnes: 2 +0 =2.\n\nTens: 9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 2 (from 292) +1 (from 5110) + 1 (carryover) =4.\n\nThousands: 0 (from 292) +5 (from 5110) =5. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
