n error in my calculation. Let me do 97*91 step by step again. \n\nLet me do 91 times 97. \n\n91 * 90 = 8190, and 91*7 = 637. Adding those together: 8190 + 637. \n\n8190 + 600 is 8790, plus 37 is 8827. \n\nSame result. So, the correct answer is 8827, not 8857. The user probably made a mistake in their initial thought. \n\nTherefore, I need to present the correct reasoning leading to 8827.\n</think>\n\n",
