.\n\n   6790.\n+    97.\n--------.\n  ?.\n\nAdding the ones place: 0 +7 =7. Tens place: 9 +9=18, so write down 8 and carry over 1. Hundreds place: 7 + 6 =13 plus the carried 1 makes 14. Thousands place: 6 remains. So putting it all together: 6 (thousands) + 1 (hundred from 14) is 7 in thousands, 4 in hundreds, 8 in tens, and 7 in ones. Wait, that might not be right. Wait, let me do it step by step:.\n\n6790 + 97:.\n\n6790.\n+  97. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
